{"title":"Perron's criterion","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Perron's Criterion states:\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/1421344b3e499d6d374983d7922855c84e46560f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\\cdots +a_1x+a_0\\in \\mathbb{Z}[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"358\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6bb078581cc43ec888a610cd77b67b697b9e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a136f78f38ddef19b8703a6a690f64cd734509.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_{n-1}|&gt;1+|a_{n-2}|+\\cdots +|a_1|+|a_0|\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is then irreducible.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perron%27s_criterion&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start of with a lemma: exactly one zero of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6fab49fad48223a8cc7418b656e5435be7b457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> and the rest satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d8a708fa8d0370f5110f4680d83eae27efed63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />.\nProof (due to Laurentiu Panaitopol): First, we will prove that no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> exists such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80488c91659d6f179f4eeec6ae9d2ad11faabfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\phi)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d19c40eeaabcc47f9c3463f932bc047fe29981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. Suppose we find such an root. Then, we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da18ab832c5c6462e25c2087c7175449ec753dd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-a_{n-1}\\phi^{n-1}=\\phi^n+a_{n-2}\\phi^{n-2}+\\cdots+a_1\\phi+a_0\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\nHowever, this means that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81395287e00e254ee92de0ff8642ab54c51871be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_{n-1}|=|a_{n-1}\\phi^{n-1}|=|\\phi^n+a_{n-2}\\phi^{n-2}+\\cdots+a_1\\phi+a_0| \\leq |\\phi^n|+|a_{n-2}\\phi^{n-2}|+\\cdots+|a_1\\phi|+|a_0|=1+|a_{n-2}|+\\cdots +|a_1|+|a_0|\\]\" width=\"889\" height=\"19\" />\nThis is a contradiction, so such a root can not exist.\n</p><p>Now, let the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b69d08c74b4b079af095bba99b43c03f96fb8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1, \\phi_2,\\cdots ,\\phi_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0cf474723b2396515745d5ff5a1781e5d271062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1\\phi_2\\cdots \\phi_n=a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, one of the roots, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2629893cf0303c8874002b5502fc0c5f521810d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />, satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/23227a284b0906b18cf7b1a7b1187a2b618b5616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi_1|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e29a15278e1ad5099acd7e797f55339e34bf5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=(x-\\phi_1)g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450b4beb445be8d63239a2129e39c02659f94ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=x^{n-1}+g_{n-2}x^{n-2}+\\cdots+g_1x+g_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7595aeb641b875ead296511a5b434b5b9c7382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=-g_0\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55c0a64d61853ec555eeebbf039771c2f0e09e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=g_{i-1}-g_{i}\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b74f72b69fbf9ce92864c5b8c25ed604613b3ec1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|b_{n-2}|+|\\phi_1|\\geq |b_{n-2}-\\phi_1|&gt;1+|b_{n-3}-b_{n-2}\\phi_1|+\\cdots+|b_0\\phi_1|\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26bf6ec4071e43373af2debfece92fa318f6dc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+|b_{n-3}-b_{n-2}\\phi_1|+\\cdots+|b_0\\phi_1|\\geq 1-|b_{n-3}|+|b_{n-2}||\\phi_1|-|b_{n-4}|+|b_{n-3}||\\phi_1|-\\cdots-|b_0|+|b_1||\\phi_1|+|b_0||\\phi_1|=1+|b_{n-2}|+(|\\phi_1|-1)(|b_{n-2}|+|b_{n-3}|+\\cdots+|b_0|)\\]\" width=\"1118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This means that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53d76ca0ea17ea07271d665b8ed481dea0cc275.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|b_{n-2}|+|b_{n-3}|+\\cdots+|b_0|&lt;1\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This means, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2a363073bdf79103c3afe54b1d316050a7c0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\rho|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efc332ff190d83da2b6f385bda7d00808be96446.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|g(\\rho)|=|\\rho^{n-1}+g_{n-2}\\rho^{n-2}+\\cdots+g_1\\rho+g_0|\\geq |\\rho|^{n-1}-(|g_{n-2}\\rho^{n-2}|+|g_{n-3}\\rho^{n-3}|+\\cdots+|g_1\\rho|+g_0|)\\geq |\\rho|^{n-1}(1-(|b_{n-2}|+|b_{n-3}|+\\cdots+|b_0|))&gt;0\\]\" width=\"1024\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, all of the other zeroes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680686f2906e8a8cc135445715c27177f3ca6adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Now, we will prove Perron's Criterion. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea1fb901c032525b58ac56d17256a25d2ba56f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=g(x)h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5547ad17b5cc1f321b2de8684cd3d134dbf39bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=x^r+g_{r-1}x^{r-1}+\\cdots+g_1x+g_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"294\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has only one root outside the unit circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2629893cf0303c8874002b5502fc0c5f521810d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />, assume that it is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Then, we get that the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc120c8302468711e6587bb2a30236b5a37d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\psi_1, \\psi_2,\\cdots,\\psi_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />, have a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e5cf33940cf0faa68bed1fe2c640a13c3de4d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" />, a nonzero integer. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2aafe28014e986bd752cedc57e798fd91398b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\psi_1\\psi_2\\cdots \\psi_r|=|g_0|&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />, a contradiction. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is irreducible.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018010021\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 125/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7599/5000000 bytes\n-->\n